Tests first (RED). Edit scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs ONLY with the main session's Edit tool (no sed, heredoc or subagent writes). task-47d21b83's plan also declares this file, so a write without a TOOL witness is HELD at landing.
(a) In test 'buildUserData renders deterministic cloud-config with a protected supervisor and locked identities' (~L1124), change the pinned line `'mounts: []'` to `'mounts: [[ephemeral0], [swap]]'`. Nothing else in that test changes.
(b) Directly after that test's closing `});`, before 'guest layout, identities and resource bounds are frozen constants shared with the launchers', add exactly the following. The architect prototyped it green in a snapshot (0.5 s):
```
// The pinned image's cloud-init 26.1 refused the old `mounts: []` (minItems 1); a schema warning ends boot "degraded done".
const CLOUD_INIT = '/usr/bin/cloud-init';
test('UD1 the emitted cloud-config passes cloud-init 26.1 schema validation with no deprecation; the old mounts: [] fails it', t => {
  const run = (...args) => spawnSync(CLOUD_INIT, args, { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 60_000, env: { PATH: '/usr/bin:/bin' } });
  const version = process.platform === 'linux' && existsSync(CLOUD_INIT) ? run('--version').stdout : null;
  if (!/^\S+ 26\.1-/.test(version ?? '')) return t.skip(`needs ${CLOUD_INIT} 26.1, found ${JSON.stringify(version?.trim() ?? null)}`);
  const dir = mkdtempSync(path.join(tmpdir(), 'moe-cloud-config-'));
  t.after(() => rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }));
  const schema = (name, text) => {
    const file = path.join(dir, name);
    writeFileSync(file, text);
    const result = run('schema', '-c', file);
    assert.equal(result.error, undefined, String(result.error));
    return { file, ...result };
  };
  const current = schema('current.yaml', BOOTSTRAP.userData);
  assert.deepEqual([current.status, current.stdout], [0, `Valid schema ${current.file}\n`], current.stderr);
  const old = BOOTSTRAP.userData.replace('\nmounts: [[ephemeral0], [swap]]\n', '\nmounts: []\n');
  assert.notEqual(old, BOOTSTRAP.userData);
  const refused = schema('old.yaml', old);
  assert.deepEqual([refused.status, refused.stdout], [1, `Invalid user-data ${refused.file}\n`], refused.stderr);
  assert.match(refused.stderr, /Cloud config schema errors: mounts: \[\] is too short/);
});
```
Every import it needs already exists: spawnSync L2, mkdtempSync/rmSync/writeFileSync L3, tmpdir L4, path L5, existsSync L278, and BOOTSTRAP is built from SUPERVISOR/CREDENTIAL at ~L928. CLOUD_INIT and the UD row prefix are unused today.
The row's error handling:
- each spawn has a 60 s timeout, and the row asserts result.error is undefined;
- the skip reason names the version found, and Windows/macOS skip before spawning anything;
- stderr is asserted only on the refused path, because WSL's cloud-init always prints a 'datasource not detected' WARNING;
- the exact stdout match on the valid path also excludes a 'Cloud config schema deprecations:' line, which matters because readiness refuses DEPRECATED recoverable errors too.
